      "parameters": {
        "toolDescription": "=Search Open Library for factual information about books.\n\nUse this tool whenever the user asks for factual information about:\n- a specific book\n- a book title\n- an author\n- an ISBN\n- publication details\n- book details\n\nThe `q` parameter must contain the most relevant search query extracted from the user's message.\n\nQuery selection:\n- For a specific book, use the book title.\n- For an author question, use the author's name.\n- For an ISBN question, use the ISBN.\n- For other book-related factual questions, use the most relevant search phrase from the user's request.\n\nThe q parameter is defined automatically by the model. Always provide the actual query value; never use placeholder text or hard-coded example values.\n\nCall this tool before answering factual questions about books.\n\nAfter receiving the results, use them to provide an accurate, concise response.\nDo not invent information that is not supported by the returned data.",
        "url": "https://openlibrary.org/search.json",
        "sendQuery": true,
